{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f7c0a6b2-9d40-4cda-9c01-7d5b1ec23a91",
    "name": "Transactions System",
    "description": "Full end-to-end test flow for the multi-tenant transaction platform.\n\nTwo distinct API key types:\n- **Source key** — held by external providers (OMT, Wish). Can POST transactions on behalf of any company via `/ingest/:sourceCode/transactions`, and discover companies via `GET /ingest/companies`.\n- **Company key** — held by the company itself. READ-ONLY. Used for programmatic dashboards/exports against `/company/*` endpoints.\n\nRun the requests **in order** from the top folder down:\n\n1. **00 — Health** — sanity check the API is up\n2. **01 — Admin** — log in as super admin, create a test company\n3. **02 — Company Owner** — log in as the new owner, create a read-only company key\n4. **02b — Admin: Source Keys** — mint a source key for a provider (e.g. OMT)\n5. **03 — Ingestion (external provider)** — discover companies, then POST a transaction using the source key + companyId\n6. **04 — Owner reads** — wallets, transactions, ledger\n7. **05 — Withdrawals** — request one, then admin approves with a reference\n8. **07 — Analytics** — admin dashboards\n9. **08 — Negative tests** — confirm validation/auth errors fire correctly\n\nThe collection has **test scripts that auto-capture** the CSRF token, company ID, owner credentials, source/company API keys, and withdrawal ID into collection variables — so you just click Send in order and everything flows.\n\n**Cookies**: Postman manages them per-host. When you switch from admin to owner login, the older session is overwritten automatically. If you want to log out fully, click the Cookies icon and clear `localhost`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3001/v1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "ali@loadless.ai", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "loadless", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "csrfToken", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "companyId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "ownerEmail", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "ownerPassword", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "apiKey", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "sourceApiKey", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "sourceCode", "value": "omt", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "sourceId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "withdrawalId", "value": "", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "transactionId", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Refresh the CSRF token variable from cookies before every request.",
          "// Mutating requests reference it via the `x-csrf-token` header.",
          "const c = pm.cookies.get('csrf-token');",
          "if (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', c);"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Also refresh CSRF after the response (Set-Cookie may have rotated it).",
          "const c = pm.cookies.get('csrf-token');",
          "if (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', c);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 — Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Sanity check. Returns `{ status: 'ok', db: 'ok' }` when Postgres is reachable."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 — Admin",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login as super admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = pm.cookies.get('csrf-token');",
                  "if (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', c);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Sets `txn_access`, `txn_refresh`, `csrf-token` cookies."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create test company",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('companyId', j.company.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('ownerEmail', j.owner.email);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('ownerPassword', j.owner.temporaryPassword);",
                  "console.log('Saved companyId =', j.company.id);",
                  "console.log('Saved ownerPassword (use it in step 02)');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-csrf-token", "value": "{{csrfToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"My Test Co\",\n  \"slug\": \"my-test-co\",\n  \"defaultCurrency\": \"USD\",\n  \"ownerEmail\": \"owner@mytestco.com\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/companies",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "companies"]
            },
            "description": "Provisions a company, an owner user, and a default-currency wallet. Auto-saves companyId + ownerPassword for the next steps.\n\nIf you re-run and get a slug conflict, change the `slug` and `ownerEmail` to fresh values."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List companies",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/companies?pageSize=20",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "companies"],
              "query": [{ "key": "pageSize", "value": "20" }]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get company by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/companies/{{companyId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "companies", "{{companyId}}"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 — Company Owner",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login as company owner",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = pm.cookies.get('csrf-token');",
                  "if (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', c);",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "console.log('Logged in as', j.email, '(mustChangePassword =', j.mustChangePassword, ')');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{ownerEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{ownerPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Overwrites the admin cookies. Subsequent cookie-authed requests are made as this company's owner.\n\n`mustChangePassword` is `true` on first login — for API testing you can ignore it, the access token still works."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "/auth/me (verify session)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create API key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('apiKey', j.plaintext);",
                  "console.log('Saved apiKey =', j.plaintext.slice(0, 24) + '…');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-csrf-token", "value": "{{csrfToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman-test\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/company/api-keys",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["company", "api-keys"]
            },
            "description": "**Read-only** company key. Use it to GET your company's transactions, wallets, ledger, withdrawals, etc. from a script or internal tool.\n\n**NOT for ingestion** — ingestion requires a source API key minted by the admin (see folder 02b — Admin: Source Keys). Attempting to POST /ingest with a company key returns 403.\n\nThe plaintext is shown **only once**. Auto-saved to {{apiKey}}."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List API keys",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/company/api-keys",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["company", "api-keys"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02b — Admin: Source Keys",
      "description": "Mint a source API key for an external provider (OMT, Wish, …). Source keys are the **only** way to POST transactions to the platform.\n\nRun the **Login as super admin** request first if your admin session expired.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "(switch to admin) Login as super admin",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const c = pm.cookies.get('csrf-token');",
                  "if (c) pm.collectionVariables.set('csrfToken', c);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "login"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List sources (find the source id for OMT)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "const wanted = pm.collectionVariables.get('sourceCode') || 'omt';",
                  "const match = (j.data || []).find(s => s.code === wanted);",
                  "if (match) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sourceId', match.id);",
                  "  console.log('Saved sourceId for', wanted, '=', match.id);",
                  "} else {",
                  "  console.warn('Could not find source code', wanted, '— pick one from the response and set {{sourceCode}} accordingly');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/sources?pageSize=100",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "sources"],
              "query": [{ "key": "pageSize", "value": "100" }]
            },
            "description": "Looks up the sourceId for `{{sourceCode}}` (default: `omt`) and saves it to `{{sourceId}}`. You can change `{{sourceCode}}` in collection variables to target any other source (wish_money_code, bank_transfer, crypto_gateway, …)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Mint source API key",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('sourceApiKey', j.plaintext);",
                  "console.log('Saved sourceApiKey =', j.plaintext.slice(0, 24) + '…');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "x-csrf-token", "value": "{{csrfToken}}" }
            ],
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"postman-source-test\"\n}" },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/sources/{{sourceId}}/api-keys",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "sources", "{{sourceId}}", "api-keys"]
            },
            "description": "Issues a fresh source-scoped API key for the source whose UUID is in `{{sourceId}}`. Auto-saves the plaintext to `{{sourceApiKey}}` for use in the ingestion folder."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List source API keys",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/sources/{{sourceId}}/api-keys",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["admin", "sources", "{{sourceId}}", "api-keys"]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 — Ingestion (external provider)",
      "description": "Run **02b — Admin: Source Keys** first to mint `{{sourceApiKey}}`. These requests use only the Bearer API key — no cookies, no CSRF. This simulates the real external integration where OMT / Wish / banks POST to the platform.\n\nKey identifies the **source**. The body's `companyId` identifies which company the transaction is **for**.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Discover companies",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "pm.test('Returns an array of companies', () => pm.expect(j.data).to.be.an('array'));",
                  "if ((j.data || []).length > 0 && !pm.collectionVariables.get('companyId')) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('companyId', j.data[0].operatingId);",
                  "  console.log('Saved operatingId =', j.data[0].operatingId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sourceApiKey}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ingest/companies",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ingest", "companies"]
            },
            "description": "External provider startup: discover the list of ACTIVE companies, cache their operatingIds. Returns `{ data: [{ operatingId, slug, name, defaultCurrency }, ...] }`. Only callable with a source key."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest 50 USD (fee 1, net 49)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.expect([200, 201]).to.include(pm.response.code));",
                  "const j = pm.response.json().data; // responses are enveloped: { success, statusCode, data }",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('transactionId', j.id);",
                  "pm.test('Fee is hidden from sources (no commissionAmount)', () => pm.expect(j).to.not.have.property('commissionAmount'));",
                  "pm.test('Net is hidden from sources (no netAmount)', () => pm.expect(j).to.not.have.property('netAmount'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sourceApiKey}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"operatingId\": \"{{companyId}}\",\n  \"externalTransactionId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}-50\",\n  \"amount\": \"50\",\n  \"currency\": \"USD\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"customer\": \"Alice (payer)\",\n    \"tradingAccount\": \"Bob (recipient)\",\n    \"phone\": \"+961-3-111-111\",\n    \"note\": \"test-from-postman\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ingest/{{sourceCode}}/transactions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ingest", "{{sourceCode}}", "transactions"]
            },
            "description": "Matches the **1–100 USD FIXED 1** seeded commission rule. The `{{$timestamp}}` keeps the externalTransactionId unique on re-run.\n\n**Payload fields** (the API recognises these plain-string fields; any extra keys are preserved):\n- `customer` — the *sender* / payer name\n- `tradingAccount` — the *recipient* / beneficiary account\n- `phone` — a contact phone number\n- `note` — free-text comment from the provider\n- any other keys under `payload` are preserved as-is"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest 200 USD (fee 5, net 195)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sourceApiKey}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"operatingId\": \"{{companyId}}\",\n  \"externalTransactionId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}-200\",\n  \"amount\": \"200\",\n  \"currency\": \"USD\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"customer\": \"Bob (payer)\",\n    \"tradingAccount\": \"Dana (recipient)\",\n    \"phone\": \"+961-3-333-333\",\n    \"note\": \"bill payment\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ingest/{{sourceCode}}/transactions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ingest", "{{sourceCode}}", "transactions"]
            },
            "description": "**101–300 USD FIXED 5** bracket."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Ingest 500 USD (2%, fee 10)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sourceApiKey}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"operatingId\": \"{{companyId}}\",\n  \"externalTransactionId\": \"postman-{{$timestamp}}-500\",\n  \"amount\": \"500\",\n  \"currency\": \"USD\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"customer\": \"Carol (payer)\",\n    \"tradingAccount\": \"Eve (recipient)\",\n    \"phone\": \"+961-3-444-444\",\n    \"note\": \"large purchase\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ingest/{{sourceCode}}/transactions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ingest", "{{sourceCode}}", "transactions"]
            },
            "description": "**301–1000 PERCENTAGE 2%** → fee 10, net 490."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Idempotency check (re-send same external id)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{sourceApiKey}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"operatingId\": \"{{companyId}}\",\n  \"externalTransactionId\": \"postman-dedup-fixed-id\",\n  \"amount\": \"50\",\n  \"currency\": \"USD\",\n  \"payload\": {}\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ingest/{{sourceCode}}/transactions",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["ingest", "{{sourceCode}}", "transactions"]
            },
            "description": "**Send this twice.** The second response should return the **same `id`** as the first — proving the dedup works. No duplicate row is created."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 — Owner reads",
      "item": [
